minimum cut value is the least capacity on its tree path, and every tree edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits the vertices into a minimum cut between its ends. Computed by Gusfield’s algorithm"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the canonical cut, vertices in order, rooted at the first: n − 1 maximum flows on one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"residual network, by push–relabel’s first phase. Disconnected graphs get zero-capacity tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The flows run in a wider type than ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where needed (","type":"text"},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int128","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for fixed-width","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integers, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"code":"Float","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so a vertex’s capacity sum may exceed ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s range.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every capacity is at least zero, not NaN and finite, and every tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"capacity (a minimum cut value) fits in "},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"GomoryHuTree.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Flows\/GomoryHuTree.swift#L20